From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: the local and loop guest-context passes respect every access to the CPU state

After 0077 PGR's home scene was still noise in two-gear mode and clean with both the local and the loop pass off (2026-11-19).
Both passes key slots by their first byte and see only the GET/PUT forms. RemoveLocalGuestContextAccesses
(InvalidateOverlappingSlots): a read pins the pending store of every slot it overlaps, a write or any other access to the CPU
state drops every mapping it overlaps, so later GETs reload. RemoveLoopGuestContextAccesses (FindUnmappableOffsets): a slot
that another access in the loop overlaps stays in memory. Applies after 0077 (ClassifyContextAccess). Not yet confirmed on
PGR with every pass on. Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/cpu_emulation/backend/include/berberis/backend/x86_64/local_guest_context_optimizer.h b/cpu_emulation/backend/include/berberis/backend/x86_64/local_guest_context_optimizer.h
index 27bbd9a..c8322e0 100644
--- a/cpu_emulation/backend/include/berberis/backend/x86_64/local_guest_context_optimizer.h
